   "title": "Unbounded response body is read fully into memory before returning",
   "evidence": "requests.get without stream=True buffers the entire body before safe_fetch returns it, and there is no Content-Length or byte cap, so an oversized or hostile response from an allowlisted (or compromised) host exhausts memory.",
